{"duration_api_ms":33641,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fa78a4da-832a-43cf-b0a4-13f51a0b7e84","total_cost_usd":0.9746714,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":104915,"cache_read_input_tokens":400677,"output_tokens":2760,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":810},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":104915,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":683,"cache_read_input_tokens":201095,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73026},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2760,"cacheReadInputTokens":400677,"cacheCreationInputTokens":104915,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9746714,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":810,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `labels/coder-1.json` (codebook 0.4, slot 1) with one row, `egi-draft-a1v2`, coded **rung 2: \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\"**\n\n- **Instrument:** AB 1955 (2023-2024), the SAFETY Act. Schiavo voted Aye on the Assembly vote to concur in Senate amendments on 2024-06-27. That was final Assembly passage of the chaptered text, and it passed 61-16.\n- **What the bill does:** Section 220.5 says schools and districts \"shall not enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches the rung-2 clause.\n- **Why not the neighbouring rungs:**\n  - **Rung 1:** the bill says staff may not be *required* to disclose. It does not require staff to keep the information from parents.\n  - **Rung 3:** that rung would require schools to tell parents who ask, which is the kind of rule Section 220.5 bars.\n- **Checks passed:**\n  - The vote is in-term (her term began 2022-12-05).\n  - About 21% voted No, so it is not near-unanimous.\n  - The other parts of the bill (parent-support resources and protection for staff) are on the same subject, so I treated it as single-subject.\n- **Fields:**\n  - The vote page carries the actor quote (\"Santiago, Schiavo, Soria\") and the tally quote (\"PASS, 61-16\").\n  - The bill-text page carries the provision quote.\n  - Both pages are in `rests_on`.\n- **Quotes:** there are none, because the sources contain no words of hers.\n- **`needs_source`:** this is empty.\n\nThe bill's wording \"unless otherwise required by state or federal law\" is the weakest point of this reading. It leaves room for a higher law to require telling parents. I still read rung 2 as met, because the bill bans exactly the local rules the rung names.","ttft_ms":14958,"type":"result","duration_ms":36642,"uuid":"a49af0ea-6765-4781-9706-a0239b92f9c5","ttft_stream_ms":7128,"time_to_request_ms":220,"first_content_frame_ms":7130,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
